# Fresora mobile client configuration.
#
# Copy to .env in this directory and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# ============================================================================
# EVERYTHING HERE IS PUBLIC
# ============================================================================
# Expo inlines every EXPO_PUBLIC_* value into the JavaScript bundle at build
# time. Anyone with the APK can read them. Never put an LLM key, a Supabase
# service-role key, or any other secret in this file -- those belong in
# backend/.env and never leave the server.
#
# After editing, restart the dev server with a cleared cache:
#   npx expo start --clear

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis API
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Base URL of the FastAPI backend, with NO trailing slash and NO /api/v1
# (the client appends the prefix itself).
#
# Leave this EMPTY for local development: the app then derives the host from
# the address Metro is already serving on and uses port 8000, which is almost
# always what you want on a physical device.
#
# "localhost" means the phone itself, not your computer, so a device on the
# same Wi-Fi needs your machine's LAN address:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.14:8000
#
# An Android emulator reaches the host machine at 10.0.2.2:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=http://10.0.2.2:8000
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (optional)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave BOTH empty to run fully on-device: inventory, scans, recipes and
# preferences are stored in AsyncStorage, there is no account, and the auth
# screens say so instead of offering a sign-in that cannot work.
#
# Set both to switch on accounts and sync. The app detects this at start-up and
# swaps its storage layer -- no code change needed.
#
# Find these under Project Settings -> API in the Supabase dashboard.
# Use the ANON / PUBLISHABLE key. The service_role key bypasses row-level
# security entirely and must never appear in this file.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
